{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/qwxm1s","slideIndex":3,"text":"IRT is Item Response Theory. The implementation uses a logistic probability based on ability theta and item difficulty. BKT is Bayesian Knowledge Tracing and maintains topic mastery probabilities. Ability theta is not a percentage. Correct answers marked Just guessing do not increase theta. Guessing receives 5% of the usual BKT update and cannot establish sufficient evidence or prerequisite readiness. These are prototype policies and require calibration with learner data. The roadmap considers all required prerequisite ancestors.\n\nSources: C:/Users/asus1/Downloads/project_synopsis.pdf, page 3. Repository: backend/app/services/irt_service.py; backend/app/services/bkt_service.py; backend/app/services/confidence_service.py; backend/README.md."}
